        "knowledge_point": "Computing a Double Summation",
        "problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$",
